"""Derive SkyyCooking/build_skyycooking_0.1.2.py from build_skyycooking_0.1.1.py (itself generated by tools/cooking_0_1_1_patch.py from
0.1): rep(old, new) with asserted anchors, newline-agnostic (the CRLF line endings of 0.1 / 0.1.1 are kept). Edit THIS patch, never the
generated build script. Run: python tools/cooking_0_1_2_patch.py, then python SkyyCooking/build_skyycooking_0.1.2.py.

0.1.2 = IN-GAME SETUP + PLAYER SETTINGS for SkyyCooking (0.1.1 is the live pin in tools/deploy_set.py):
 - research/Server-Setup-Spec.md 4.13 + 7 (tools/CONFIG-CONTRACT.md): the tools/skyycfg.py kit. config:def:SkyyCooking + config:fn:SkyyCooking
   (+ config:epoch) published at the END of setup() after CookCfg.load(); node skyycooking.admin (the existing admin node); file
   Skyy_SkyyCooking/cooking.properties with its keys unchanged; every row binds reload: (the kit rewrites only the changed line, then runs
   CookCfg.load(), the routine /cookadmin reload already used). Rows: enabled (part), maxGrade, graded (+ check hook: only dishes with
   Grade assets), creativeGrades (danger, confirm=on), xpMultiplier (danger), maxXpPerMinute, table xp (xp.<output id>; its "default" entry
   IS xp.default), campfire.buffFactor, campfire.xpFactor, table tree (tree.<Node>.per, adv), messages.
   /cookadmin reload keeps working and now goes through the kit (pending in-game changes flushed, hand edits logged via=file), then
   re-reads the file as before; /cookadmin give / campfire write no config and are unchanged.
 - research/Settings-Spec.md 1.3 + 3.6 (the "next: 0.1.2" there happens to match the live 0.1.1 + 1): Cook.notifyOn / Cook.regSetting
   (mod "SkyyCooking"), a 4-argument Cook.tell (the setting check sits BEFORE the LAST throttle, so a hidden line does not eat the 2.5 s
   cooldown; the 3-argument tell delegates with key null), gates: Grade-up line + campfire hint -> cooking.grade, proc note -> cooking.procs.
   TOLD / CAMP_TOLD are still written before the gated call (a hidden Grade counts as told). Both switches registered in setup().
 - Default behaviour is identical: every row default equals the value the generated cooking.properties writes (build-checked), no
   gameplay code changed, and without SkyyMenu every switch reads ON.
Full contract: the 0.1.2 section at the top of the generated script's docstring.
"""
import os
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
src = os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyCooking", "build_skyycooking_0.1.1.py")
dst = os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyCooking", "build_skyycooking_0.1.2.py")
raw = open(src, encoding="utf8", newline="").read()
CR, LF = chr(13), chr(10)
NL = CR + LF if (CR + LF) in raw else LF
s = raw.replace(CR + LF, LF)


def rep(old, new):
    global s
    n = s.count(old)
    assert n == 1, "anchor count %d: %s" % (n, old[:120])
    s = s.replace(old, new, 1)


